    "description": "Deletions or point mutations in the duplicated HBA1 and HBA2 genes reduce or abolish alpha-globin chain synthesis. The resulting excess of unpaired beta-globin chains forms unstable hemoglobin H tetramers that precipitate and damage red cells, producing chronic hemolytic anemia and ineffective erythropoiesis. Disease severity scales with the number of affected alpha-globin alleles, ranging from silent carriage to hemoglobin H disease and lethal hemoglobin Bart hydrops fetalis.",
