    "description": "Asthma is a chronic inflammatory disease of the airways characterized by variable, reversible airflow obstruction, bronchial hyperresponsiveness, and airway remodeling. In the common type 2-high form, allergen sensitization drives a Th2 and innate lymphoid cell response with IL-4, IL-5, and IL-13 that recruits eosinophils, promotes IgE production and mast cell activation, and induces mucus hypersecretion; type 2-low (neutrophilic or paucigranulocytic) endotypes also occur. Episodic exposure to triggers such as allergens, viral infection, exercise, or irritants provokes smooth muscle bronchoconstriction, airway edema, and mucus plugging, producing recurrent wheeze, cough, chest tightness, and dyspnea, with chronic inflammation leading to remodeling over time.",
