    "description": "Atopic dermatitis is a chronic, relapsing inflammatory skin disease arising from the combination of epidermal barrier dysfunction and type 2-skewed immune dysregulation. Loss-of-function variants in filaggrin and related barrier defects increase transepidermal water loss and allow penetration of allergens and microbes, while keratinocyte-derived alarmins (TSLP, IL-25, IL-33) drive Th2 responses with IL-4, IL-13, and IL-31 that further impair barrier proteins and lipids and mediate pruritus. The resulting itch-scratch cycle, skin dysbiosis with Staphylococcus aureus overgrowth, and sustained inflammation produce the eczematous, lichenified, intensely pruritic lesions, often as part of the broader atopic march.",
