    "description": "Burkitt lymphoma is a highly aggressive B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma characterized by MYC oncogene translocation, typically t(8;14)(q24;q32) involving the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus. Three clinical variants exist: endemic (African), sporadic, and immunodeficiency-associated. Endemic Burkitt lymphoma is strongly associated with Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) infection and commonly presents as jaw tumors in children in malaria-endemic regions. The disease exemplifies the role of MYC dysregulation in driving exceptionally rapid cell proliferation and clinical progression.",
