    "description": "Cough variant asthma is a phenotype of asthma in which chronic dry cough is the sole or predominant symptom, without the wheeze and dyspnea of classic asthma. It shares the underlying eosinophilic airway inflammation and bronchial hyperresponsiveness of typical asthma, but the airway narrowing and cough reflex sensitization are insufficient to produce overt wheeze. Diagnosis rests on demonstrating reversible airflow limitation or airway hyperresponsiveness and a response to bronchodilator and inhaled corticosteroid therapy, and a substantial proportion of untreated patients progress to classic asthma.",
