    "description": "Cytomegalovirus (CMV) retinitis is a sight-threatening opportunistic infection of the retina caused by reactivation of latent cytomegalovirus in immunocompromised hosts, most classically people with advanced HIV/AIDS and low CD4 counts, as well as transplant and immunosuppressed patients. Productive CMV infection produces a progressive, full-thickness necrotizing retinitis that can rapidly lead to retinal detachment and irreversible blindness if untreated. It is historically notable as the indication for fomivirsen, the first antisense oligonucleotide drug ever approved by the FDA (1998).",
