    "description": "Dacryocystitis-osteopoikilosis syndrome is a rare autosomal dominant disorder in which recurrent dacryocystitis from nasolacrimal duct obstruction co-occurs with osteopoikilosis, a sclerosing bone dysplasia of multiple small foci of trabecular bone. It is caused by loss-of-function variants in LEMD3, the same gene underlying osteopoikilosis and Buschke-Ollendorff syndrome; LEMD3 antagonizes BMP and TGF-beta signaling, and its loss leads to excess bone morphogenetic signaling and focal osteosclerosis. The associated lacrimal drainage anomaly produces tearing and recurrent infection of the lacrimal sac, linking the skeletal and ophthalmic manifestations within a single developmental disorder.",
    "pathophysiology": [
      "LEMD3/MAN1 Loss-of-Function and Dysregulated TGF-beta/BMP Signaling",
      "Focal Osteosclerosis (Osteopoikilosis)",
      "Lacrimal Canal Stenosis"
    ],
