    "description": "Ebola virus disease (EVD) is a severe, frequently fatal viral hemorrhagic fever caused by ebolaviruses (family Filoviridae), most lethally Zaire ebolavirus, transmitted to humans from an animal reservoir and then between people through contact with infected body fluids. The virus enters cells by macropinocytosis and NPC1-dependent endosomal fusion, replicates broadly in macrophages, dendritic cells, and endothelium, and uses proteins such as VP35 and VP24 to suppress interferon responses. Widespread immune dysregulation, endothelial dysfunction with vascular leak, and consumptive coagulopathy (disseminated intravascular coagulation) drive shock, multiorgan failure, and hemorrhage.",
