    "description": "Epilepsy is a chronic neurological disorder defined by an enduring predisposition to recurrent unprovoked seizures arising from abnormal, excessive, and synchronous neuronal activity. It encompasses focal and generalized syndromes (e.g., temporal lobe epilepsy, juvenile myoclonic epilepsy, childhood absence epilepsy). The core mechanism is an imbalance between neuronal excitation and inhibition producing hyperexcitability and hypersynchrony, driven by ion-channel, synaptic, and network dysfunction.",
