    "description": "Familial Mediterranean fever is caused by MEFV mutations that yield dysfunctional pyrin and lower the threshold for pyrin inflammasome activation. Loss of the RhoA-PKN regulatory checkpoint permits inappropriate inflammasome assembly, caspase-1 activation, and gasdermin D-mediated pyroptosis with IL-1beta release. The result is recurrent, self-limited attacks of fever and serositis driven by uncontrolled innate immune inflammation.",
