    "description": "Fibromyalgia is characterized by central sensitization, in which augmented central pain processing with elevated excitatory neurotransmitters amplifies pain perception. Impaired descending inhibition from reduced serotonin and norepinephrine, neuroinflammatory glial activation, HPA-axis dysregulation, and small-fiber pathology compound the heightened pain sensitivity. These mechanisms produce widespread chronic musculoskeletal pain accompanied by fatigue, sleep disturbance, and cognitive symptoms.",
