    "description": "Glaucoma is a group of progressive optic neuropathies characterized by retinal ganglion cell death and degeneration of the optic nerve, producing characteristic cupping of the optic disc and corresponding visual field loss. Elevated intraocular pressure, usually from impaired aqueous humor outflow through the trabecular meshwork (open-angle) or from physical closure of the drainage angle (angle-closure), is the principal modifiable risk factor that drives mechanical and ischemic stress at the optic nerve head. Because the ganglion cell loss is irreversible and often asymptomatic until advanced, glaucoma is a leading cause of irreversible blindness worldwide.",
