    "description": "Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy (HCM) is the most common inherited cardiomyopathy, typically caused by autosomal dominant mutations in sarcomere protein genes. It is characterized by left ventricular hypertrophy not explained by loading conditions, with myocyte disarray and interstitial fibrosis. Asymmetric septal hypertrophy can produce dynamic left ventricular outflow tract obstruction; HCM is a leading cause of sudden cardiac death in young people.",
