    "description": "Labyrinthitis is an inflammation of the membranous labyrinth of the inner ear that affects both the vestibular and cochlear end organs, distinguishing it from vestibular neuritis, which spares hearing. It most often follows a viral infection, though bacterial spread from otitis media or meningitis can cause a suppurative form; inflammation and the resulting disturbance of inner ear fluid homeostasis impair function of the hair cells and vestibular and cochlear nerves. The acute loss of unilateral vestibular input produces vertigo, nausea, and nystagmus, while cochlear involvement adds hearing loss and tinnitus, with central compensation driving gradual recovery.",
