    "description": "McKusick-Kaufman syndrome (MKKS) is an autosomal recessive multiple congenital anomaly syndrome classically comprising the triad of hydrometrocolpos, postaxial polydactyly, and congenital heart disease. It is caused by biallelic variants in the MKKS gene, which is the same chaperonin-like BBSome assembly gene known as BBS6. McKusick-Kaufman syndrome is therefore allelic to Bardet-Biedl syndrome 6 and is a \"BBSome-opathy\": on the shared BBSome trafficking pathway it represents the limb (Hedgehog) and genitourinary developmental branches, classically without the retinal dystrophy and obesity that define Bardet-Biedl syndrome. Because the two conditions overlap, an early McKusick-Kaufman diagnosis can be reclassified as Bardet-Biedl syndrome once retinopathy or obesity emerge on follow-up.",
    "pathophysiology": [
      "MKKS chaperonin assembly defect",
      "Defective BBSome assembly",
      "BBSome-dependent ciliary cargo trafficking failure",
      "Altered Sonic hedgehog-dependent limb patterning",
      "Genitourinary developmental defect",
      "Non-ciliary BBS6 nuclear-cytoplasmic transport defect"
    ],
