    "description": "Monkeypox (mpox) is a zoonotic viral illness caused by the monkeypox virus, a double-stranded DNA orthopoxvirus related to variola (smallpox) virus, with West African and more virulent Central African (Congo Basin) clades. After entry through skin, mucosa, or the respiratory tract, the virus replicates in cytoplasmic viral factories, spreads via lymphatics and a hematogenous viremia, and produces multiple immune-evasion proteins that blunt host interferon and complement responses. Clinically it causes fever, lymphadenopathy, and a characteristic centrifugal vesiculopustular rash that progresses through synchronous lesion stages.",
