    "description": "Multiple system atrophy (MSA) is a sporadic, rapidly progressive adult-onset neurodegenerative disorder combining autonomic failure with parkinsonism (MSA-P) and/or cerebellar ataxia (MSA-C). It is an alpha-synucleinopathy defined pathologically by glial cytoplasmic inclusions of misfolded alpha-synuclein in oligodendrocytes, leading to demyelination and widespread neuronal loss across striatonigral, olivopontocerebellar, and autonomic systems.",
