    "description": "Niemann-Pick disease type C is an autosomal recessive lysosomal lipid storage disorder caused by pathogenic variants in NPC1 (the large majority of cases) or NPC2, which encode proteins required for egress of unesterified cholesterol and other lipids from late endosomes and lysosomes. The resulting accumulation of unesterified cholesterol, glycosphingolipids, and sphingosine impairs autophagy and lysosomal calcium handling and drives progressive neurodegeneration, including cerebellar Purkinje cell loss. Clinical hallmarks include hepatosplenomegaly, vertical supranuclear gaze palsy, cerebellar ataxia, dysphagia, dystonia, gelastic cataplexy, and progressive cognitive decline.",
