    "description": "Nipah virus disease is a zoonotic infection caused by Nipah virus, a henipavirus in the family Paramyxoviridae, whose natural reservoir is fruit bats of the genus Pteropus. Human infection follows exposure to infected bats, intermediate hosts such as pigs, or food contaminated with bat secretions (notably raw date palm sap), and produces a severe febrile illness that can progress to encephalitis, respiratory distress, and death with high case-fatality.",
