    "description": "Phenylketonuria is an autosomal recessive inborn error of amino acid metabolism caused by biallelic pathogenic variants in PAH that reduce or abolish hepatic phenylalanine hydroxylase activity, the enzyme that converts phenylalanine to tyrosine. The resulting hyperphenylalaninemia, with relative tyrosine deficiency, impairs large neutral amino acid transport across the blood-brain barrier and monoamine neurotransmitter synthesis, causing brain phenylalanine toxicity. If untreated, it leads to intellectual disability, seizures, microcephaly, hypopigmentation, and a musty body odor; newborn screening and a phenylalanine-restricted diet, supplemented in responsive patients by sapropterin (tetrahydrobiopterin) or pegvaliase, prevent the neurocognitive sequelae.",
