    "description": "Primary hyperoxaluria type 2 (PH2) is an autosomal recessive disorder of hepatic glyoxylate metabolism caused by biallelic GRHPR pathogenic variants. Deficient glyoxylate reductase/hydroxypyruvate reductase activity reduces glyoxylate-to-glycolate and hydroxypyruvate-to-D-glycerate flux, causing increased urinary oxalate and L-glycerate. Increased oxalate excretion drives calcium oxalate nephrolithiasis, nephrocalcinosis, and in some individuals kidney failure with systemic oxalate deposition.",
