    "description": "Psoriasis is a chronic immune-mediated inflammatory skin disease driven by a self-amplifying loop centered on the IL-23/Th17 axis. In genetically predisposed individuals (notably HLA-C*06:02 carriers), activated dendritic cells secrete IL-23, which expands Th17 cells that release IL-17A and IL-22; these cytokines drive keratinocyte hyperproliferation, abnormal differentiation, and production of further chemokines and antimicrobial peptides that recruit neutrophils and sustain the inflammatory circuit. The result is the characteristic well-demarcated, erythematous, silvery-scaled plaques, with associated nail disease and psoriatic arthritis in a substantial subset of patients.",
