    "description": "Rheumatoid arthritis is a systemic autoimmune disease in which loss of tolerance, often heralded by ACPA and rheumatoid factor autoantibodies, targets the synovial membrane. Overproduction of TNF-alpha, IL-1, and IL-6 sustains synovial inflammation, with JAK/STAT and NF-kB signaling and metabolic reprogramming amplifying immune and fibroblast activation. Inflammatory synovial hyperplasia forms an invasive pannus that erodes articular cartilage and underlying bone, producing joint destruction.",
