    "description": "SECISBP2 deficiency is an autosomal recessive inborn error of selenoprotein synthesis caused by biallelic SECISBP2 variants. SECISBP2/SBP2 is part of the SECIS-recognition machinery that recodes UGA codons for selenocysteine insertion, so partial loss of function reduces synthesis of many human selenoproteins. The downstream pathograph includes impaired deiodinase-driven thyroid hormone metabolism, oxidative-stress vulnerability from antioxidant selenoprotein deficiency, growth failure with delayed bone maturation, and variable neurodevelopmental involvement.",
