    "description": "SEPSECS deficiency is an autosomal recessive selenocysteine biosynthesis disorder caused by biallelic SEPSECS variants. SEPSECS (O-phosphoseryl-tRNA:selenocysteinyl-tRNA synthase) catalyzes the final conversion of Sep-tRNA(Sec) to Sec-tRNA(Sec), the only route to human selenoprotein generation. Disruption of this step produces a severe neurodevelopmental and neurodegenerative phenotype, classically progressive cerebello-cerebral atrophy or pontocerebellar hypoplasia type 2D, with profound developmental delay, microcephaly, hypotonia evolving to spasticity, and progressive cerebellar atrophy.",
