    "description": "Salla disease is an autosomal recessive free sialic acid storage disorder caused by pathogenic variants in SLC17A5, which encodes sialin, the lysosomal membrane transporter that exports free sialic acid from the lysosome. Loss of sialin function causes free sialic acid to accumulate within lysosomes, producing oligodendroglial dysfunction with central hypomyelination and progressive neurodegeneration. Affected individuals present with infantile-onset hypotonia, developmental delay, intellectual disability, ataxia, nystagmus, and spasticity, with corpus callosum hypoplasia and hypomyelination on neuroimaging; it lies on a severity continuum with the more severe infantile free sialic acid storage disorder.",
