    "description": "Spinal muscular atrophy (SMA) is an autosomal recessive neuromuscular disorder caused by biallelic loss of the SMN1 gene, leading to deficiency of the survival motor neuron (SMN) protein and degeneration of alpha motor neurons in the anterior horn of the spinal cord. This produces progressive, symmetric proximal muscle weakness and atrophy. Disease severity, classified into types 1-4, correlates inversely with the copy number of the modifying SMN2 gene.",
