    "description": "Tay-Sachs disease is an autosomal recessive GM2 gangliosidosis caused by biallelic pathogenic variants in HEXA, which encodes the alpha subunit of the lysosomal enzyme beta-hexosaminidase A. Deficient hexosaminidase A activity blocks degradation of GM2 ganglioside, which accumulates progressively within neurons and triggers neuroinflammation and neuronal death. The classic infantile form presents with developmental regression, hypotonia, an exaggerated startle response, a macular cherry-red spot, seizures, and blindness, while juvenile and late-onset forms with residual enzyme activity follow a more protracted course dominated by ataxia and motor neuron involvement.",
