    "description": "Trisomy 18 (Edwards syndrome) is a common autosomal trisomy caused by the presence of an extra chromosome 18 \u2014 full trisomy in most cases, or mosaic or partial trisomy 18q. It is the second most common autosomal trisomy syndrome after trisomy 21. Whole-chromosome gene-dosage imbalance disrupts development across multiple organ systems, producing prenatal and postnatal growth deficiency, characteristic craniofacial features, a clenched hand with overriding fingers, major malformations (most often cardiac and renal), consistent feeding problems, and marked psychomotor and cognitive disability. Neonatal and infant mortality is high, though a minority of children survive beyond the first year.",
