    "description": "VPS51-related pontocerebellar hypoplasia-CDG is a rare autosomal recessive neurodevelopmental and neurometabolic disorder caused by biallelic VPS51 variants. VPS51 encodes the shared GARP/EARP tethering-complex subunit needed for endosome-derived carrier fusion at the trans-Golgi network and recycling endosomes. Patient cells show reduced assembled GARP/EARP complexes, altered mannose-6-phosphate receptor distribution, lysosomal swelling, and abnormal cellular and serum glycoprotein glycosylation. Reported individuals have severe developmental delay or intellectual disability, microcephaly, epilepsy, hypotonia, thin corpus callosum or pontocerebellar abnormalities, failure to thrive, and variable hepatic, hearing, feeding, and vision involvement.",
